--- !u!114 &462517331408017837
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1192497626828263742}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b77fdcd59c531ba40a1fe73f7ec53642, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ZoomScreenShareController
  incomingCallPopup: {fileID: 6841482942641554163}
  zoomPanel: {fileID: 9189870688026870596}
  screensharePopup: {fileID: 8552603436118496086}
  screenShareDisplay: {fileID: 0}
  screenShareVideoPlayer: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueCues:
  - triggerTimestampSeconds: 3
    pauseVideo: 0
    dialogue:
      speakerName: Steve
      personality: 0
      text: "Alright, first things first\u2014head over to sfml-dev.org and download the SFML 3 package that matches your C++ toolchain."
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayDuration: 14
  - triggerTimestampSeconds: 19
    pauseVideo: 0
    dialogue:
      speakerName: Steve
      personality: 0
      text: Then, you can just export it/unzip the libary folder
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayDuration: 10
  - triggerTimestampSeconds: 30
    pauseVideo: 1
    dialogue:
      speakerName: The Architect
      personality: 2
      text: Notice how he extracts the library directly into an external/ directory inside the project root. Keeping third-party libraries localized avoids dirtying global system paths
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayDuration: 10
  - triggerTimestampSeconds: 31
    pauseVideo: 1
    dialogue:
      speakerName: The Pragmatist
      personality: 3
      text: Who cares...
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayDuration: 1.8
  - triggerTimestampSeconds: 33
    pauseVideo: 0
    dialogue:
      speakerName: Steve
      personality: 0
      text: Alright, so when you make your new CLion Project, make sure to use C++17 or 20
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayDuration: 7
  - triggerTimestampSeconds: 40
    pauseVideo: 1
    dialogue:
      speakerName: Steve
      personality: 0
      text: And always make sure your project and all its dependencies finish loading before doing anything.
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayDuration: 10
  - triggerTimestampSeconds: 51
    pauseVideo: 0
    dialogue:
      speakerName: Steve
      personality: 0
      text: Open CMakeLists.txt. We'll set SFML_DIR to point to our external/SFML folder, then use find_package() to pull in Graphics, Audio, Window, and System
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayDuration: 10
  - triggerTimestampSeconds: 130
    pauseVideo: 1
    dialogue:
      speakerName: The Sentinel
      personality: 4
      text: Pay attention to target_link_libraries. Linking SFML targets directly to your executable scope ensures proper symbol resolution and prevents runtime memory leaks from dangling dependencies
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayDuration: 10
  - triggerTimestampSeconds: 137
    pauseVideo: 1
    dialogue:
      speakerName: Steve
      personality: 0
      text: And that should be it! Please correct me if I did anything wrong sir. I'm here to learn from you
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayDuration: 5
  - triggerTimestampSeconds: 138
    pauseVideo: 1
    dialogue:
      speakerName: The Pragmatist
      personality: 3
      text: 'Whatever, I''m sure we could''ve just asked chatpgt '
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayDuration: 5
  - triggerTimestampSeconds: 138.5
    pauseVideo: 1
    dialogue:
      speakerName: The Detective
      personality: 6
      text: Maybe we could ask this Mr.GPT who we are? He seems like a well-informed fellow
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayDuration: 5
